==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[:w:Tuxedo Park, New York|Tuxedo Park, New York]], USA, where the fashion is often said to have originated, the village in turn likely from an {{der|en|alg-eas}} language ({{der|en|umu|-}}), from [[Lenape]], [[tucsedo]] or [[p'tuxseepu]], ("crooked water" or "crooked river").

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|tŭksē'dō}}, {{IPA|en|/tʌkˈsidoʊ/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/tʌkˈsiːdəʊ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tuxedo.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːdəʊ|s=3}}

===Noun===
[[Image:Men in black tie.jpg|thumb|right|Three men in tuxedos]]
{{en-noun|s|tuxedoes}}

# A typically [[black]] [[formal]] [[jacket]] worn by men.
# The entire [[suit]] complementing and including this jacket.
# {{ellipsis of|en|tuxedo cat}}

